{"created": 1791911293006, "completed": 1791911337338}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_1363c704e002zbgyoYcsF3J5mm", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "9c9ac675d4960b72ffd21d7a0bce04fe40c9a514", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_1363c740d001o0CsGQiuH5QKHX", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1363c704e002zbgyoYcsF3J5mm"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "Good:\n- FastVocab parts are tiny (108K total) — the 7g daemon heap was only because of RuWordList. After removing 603 giant files, I can reduce kotlin.daemon.jvmargs back to 3g and update the comment.\n- baseline profiles don't reference RuWordList.\n- logcat style: `import logcat.LogPriority` + `import tachiyomi.core.common.util.system.logcat`.\n\nNow let me implement.\n\nStep 1: Generate the asset file from the existing .kt parts (source of truth = current repo state = the exact 3,014,492 forms). I'll write a small throwaway python to produce `data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt` (uppercase, sorted, unique). Then verify count.\n\nStep 2: Rewrite RuWordList.kt.\n\nStep 3: Delete RuWordListPart*.kt.\n\nStep 4: Wire App.kt.\n\nStep 5: Update gen_ruwordlist.py to emit the asset instead of .kt parts.\n\nStep 6: Update gradle.properties heap + comment.\n\nStep 7: Build/test.\n\nLet me generate the asset file first.\n\nNote: file content should match exactly what RuWordList.upper currently builds = { w.uppercase() for w in parts }. Since generator stored lower forms (with ё→е). So uppercase of each stored form. I'll parse all part .kt files, take the string literals, uppercase, dedupe, sort.\n\nWait — careful: the part .kt files contain ONLY the word strings (plus header comments). My earlier extraction regex `\"([^\"]+)\"` with cyrillic filter found 3,014,492 forms unique uppercase. Let me generate with the same extraction but WITHOUT the cyrillic-only filter (in case some words contain hyphen or digits?). Earlier filter was `[А-ЯЁа-яё]+` and found 3,014,492 matches where raw utf8 was 67.8MB. But some forms may contain hyphens (gen builds allow hyphen). Earlier regex fullmatch `[А-ЯЁа-яё]+` excluded hyphenated words! But count matched 3,014,492 exactly, so apparently the current parts happen to have no hyphens, or hyphenated ones are separate literal lines that my regex (`\"([^\"]+)\"` + fullmatch cyrillic) missed and counted lower. Hmm — my earlier count got 3,014,492 matching the declared size. But int literals in the file also might match? No, fullmatch cyrillic excludes. Let me just pull ALL string literals from the part files (format: `    \"WORD\",`) to be exhaustive and dedupe by uppercase. Better to replicate RuWordList exactly: for each literal, uppercase. Use python extraction of all `\"...\"` literals.\n\nLet me write the generator:\n\n```python\nimport glob, re\nlines = set()\nfor f in glob.glob('data/src/main/java/mihon/data/ocr/RuWordListPart*.kt'):\n    txt = open(f, encoding='utf-8').read()\n    for m in re.findall(r'\"([^\"]*)\"', txt):\n        if m:\n            lines.add(m.upper())\nout = sorted(lines)\nprint(len(out))\nwith open('data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt','w',encoding='utf-8',newline='\\n') as h:\n    for w in out:\n        h.write(w+'\\n')\n```\n\nWait newline issue: on windows, '\\n' writes CRLF unless newline='' or newline='\\n' set. Use newline='\\n' explicitly to force LF. This is important for deterministic bytes + kotlin readLine handling (readLine handles \\r\\n? BufferedReader.readLine strips line terminators including \\r\\n. Still normalization matters for deterministic asset). Use newline='\\n'.\n\nThen verify size == 3_014_492 and gzip of content ~8.6MB (informational).\n\nBut — one important check: current RuWordList.upper does `w.uppercase()` with the *default locale* in Kotlin/Java on device. My python `.upper()` is locale-independent (unicode-aware) for Cyrillic — same result. For 'ё' → 'Ё'. Same. For any latin? Possibly some forms contain latin? gen only allowed Cyrillic + hyphen + ё. So fine.\n\nAlso includes the single-letter service words А, В, И, К, О, С, У, Я (uppercase already in seeds) — they're in parts presumably. The build set includes them. Good.\n\nStep 2: RuWordList.kt new content:\n\n```kotlin\npackage mihon.data.ocr\n\nimport android.content.Context\nimport java.io.File\nimport java.io.InputStream\nimport logcat.LogPriority\nimport tachiyomi.core.common.util.system.logcat\n\n/**\n * Частотный словарь русских словоформ для разбиения слипшегося OCR-текста...\n * (keep KDoc, but update about storage)\n */\nobject RuWordList {\n\n    private const val ASSET_PATH = \"ocr/ru_wordlist.txt\"\n\n    private const val EXPECTED_FORMS = 3_014_492\n\n    @Volatile\n    private var opener: (() -> InputStream)? = null\n\n    /** Привязывает словарь к ассету приложения. Вызывается на старте (App). */\n    fun configure(context: Context) {\n        opener = { context.assets.open(ASSET_PATH) }\n    }\n\n    private fun openSource(): InputStream? {\n        opener?.let { return it() }\n        // JVM-юнит-тесты не имеют AssetManager: читаем файл из исходников модуля\n        // (Gradle запускает тесты с рабочим каталогом = каталог модуля).\n        for (path in TEST_SOURCE_CANDIDATES) {\n            val file = File(path)\n            if (file.isFile) return file.inputStream()\n        }\n        return null\n    }\n\n    private val TEST_SOURCE_CANDIDATES = listOf(\n        \"src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt\",\n        \"data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt\",\n    )\n\n    /** Словоформы ВЕРХНИМ регистром: прогоны OCR приходят капсом. */\n    val upper: Set<String> by lazy(LazyThreadSafetyMode.SYNCHRONIZED) {\n        val stream = openSource()\n        if (stream == null) {\n            logcat(LogPriority.WARN) { \"RuWordList: словарь не найден — разбиение капса будет работать хуже\" }\n            return@lazy emptySet()\n        }\n        stream.bufferedReader(Charsets.UTF_8).use { reader ->\n            // Формы в файле уже прописные; точный capacity — без рехэширования.\n            val set = HashSet<String>((EXPECTED_FORMS / 0.75f).toInt() + 1)\n            var line: String? = reader.readLine()\n            while (line != null) {\n                if (line.isNotEmpty()) set.add(line)\n                line = reader.readLine()\n            }\n            set\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nWait — `var line: String?` — readLine returns String?. And java BufferedReader.readLine() returns String (nullable). Kotlin type is String?. Good.\n\nBut `stream.bufferedReader(Charsets.UTF_8).use` — use on the reader; `.use` returns the result of block = set. Good.\n\nHowever `HashSet<String>(capacity)` — Kotlin/Java HashSet(int) → initial capacity. Good.\n\nEdge: `reader.use { ... set }` returns set. \n\nThe `upper` type: `Set<String>` — previously it was HashSet as Set<String>. Fine.\n\nBut lazy + assignment from build: `by lazy(LazyThreadSafetyMode.SYNCHRONIZED)`.\n\nOne concern: `openSource()` opens the file stream each lazy init only once (lazy caches). Good.\n\nWait, there's a subtle problem with `configure(context)` capturing the Application context: it's an OK pattern (Application context, no leak). App.kt has applicationContext.\n\nNow — is `upper` accessed a lot concurrently? Dictionary during OCR runs from worker threads; lazy SYNCHRONIZED initializes once safely. Good. After init, HashSet reads are not thread-safe in general but we only read (contains) — concurrent reads of a non-modified HashMap/HashSet are safe. Today same. Parity.\n\nAlso remove KDoc about parts files and mention asset + gen script. Update the class KDoc first part: keep the description (frequency dictionary purpose + sources), adapt the storage/dimensions paragraph (\"Размер словаря...\" keep) and remove the \"Файлы кладутся ...\" from gen script doc.\n\nAlso — does anything else import `ruWordListPart*`? grep for that exact name across repo.\n\nStep 3: delete part files.\n\nStep 4: App.kt add call.\n\nStep 5: gen_ruwordlist.py — rewrite the emission section (write_parts/sync_parts_list) to `write_asset()`. Keep `build()` same (lowercase forms). The asset content = sorted forms, UPPERCASE. So:\n\n```python\ndef write_asset(repo, forms):\n    out_dir = os.path.join(repo, \"data/src/main/assets/ocr\")\n    os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    path = os.path.join(out_dir, \"ru_wordlist.txt\")\n    # Формы пишем прописными: [RuWordList.upper] вставляет строки как есть,\n    # без 3 млн uppercase() на старте.\n    with open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\\n\") as handle:\n        for word in forms:\n            handle.write(word.upper() + \"\\n\")\n    return path\n```\n\nAnd main():\n\n```python\ndef main():\n    lexicon_path, repo = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]\n    forms = build(lexicon_path, repo)\n    path = write_asset(repo, forms)\n    print(f\"форм: {len(forms)}, ассет: {path}\")\n```\n\nUpdate docstring.\n\nAlso remove references to REPO_OCR_DIR/RULIST_KT/PART_SIZE? Keep PART_SIZE? No longer needed. Remove write_parts, sync_parts_list, and RULIST_KT const. Keep REPO_OCR_DIR? repo_forms() reads old parts to carry over — but comment says old list no longer pulled. Actually repo_forms is defined but unused in build()? Let me check: `build()` doesn't call repo_forms. repo_forms defined but unused (dead). I'll remove it too? It was possibly legacy. Keep the change minimal but clean: remove repo_forms, write_parts, sync_parts_list, and their constants; add write_asset.\n\nAlso update the module docstring from \"Файлы кладутся в ... RuWordListPartNNN.kt\" to asset description.\n\nStep 6: gradle.properties: set kotlin.daemon.jvmargs back to -Xmx3g and update the comment to explain that a big embedded dictionary previously needed 7g; now it lives as an asset so compiler doesn't need the heap. Wait — will 3g suffice? The Kotlin compiler previously needed 7g because of 3M string literals in 603 files. Now removed. Other modules unchanged from the \"было 3g\" era. But vocabFastPart is made of 2 files (0.3MB). So 3g is fine. I'll set 3g with updated comment.\n\nActually be cautious: \"kotlin.daemon.jvmargs\" bump was a workaround; if 3g breaks compile of something else (the 7g era also coincided with general growth), the original setting was 3g before. I'll set 3g as it was \"было\". If build fails, revert to 7g. The change is in build config — user said don't degrade; this speeds up builds. It's optional. I'll do it but carefully; build will verify.\n\nHmm, but is it wise to touch gradle.properties during this task? Risk is low and it's directly related (the 7g bump was caused by the dictionary we're removing). If :data compiles fine, keep. I'll test the whole assemble.\n\nStep 7: Run tests: `./gradlew :data:testDebugUnitTest` — wait, is it debug unit test variant? For library, testDebugUnitTest exists. Also spotless. And assembleDebug? The app assembleDebug would include asset merging — important to verify APK. But assembleDebug might take long (this is a huge project). Let me at least run the data unit tests and compileDebugKotlin for app? Building full app may exceed time but let's try `:app:assembleDebug` — could be long. Let me start with data tests, then app assemble if time permits.\n\nActually the asset lives in the data module & is read by data module code. The app module just calls configure. To verify asset merges into APK correctly, assembleDebug or `:app:mergeDebugAssets`/`packageDebug` and inspect APK size. Let me plan: run `:data:testDebugUnitTest` and `:app:assembleDebug` (with long timeout). Also spotlessCheck for changed files.\n\nLet me also verify there are no other references to RuWordListPart after deletion.\n\nLet me now start implementing. First generate asset file.\n\nAlso: I need to double check there isn't an existing `.editorconfig` or spotless rule that would reformat the .txt (no, binary/text asset untouched by spotless).\n\nAlso check: `data/src/main/assets/` exists (`panel_detector`). Create `ocr/`.\n\nLet me write the generation script as a throwaway and run it. Then verify size + gzip.\n\nOne more consideration — file line ending: use \"\\n\" only.\n\nAlso there might be trailing spaces? No.\n\nLet me produce the file and verify count 3,014,492 and that file's gz ≈ 8-9MB. \n\nThen implement code changes.\n\nRegarding order: implement RuWordList.kt after generating asset (so tests can run). Delete .kt parts AFTER verifying tests pass with new object? If I delete first, tests won't compile until new object in place. I'll rewrite RuWordList.kt first, then build & test with parts still present? No — new RuWordList no longer references parts, but parts files still exist (compiled but unused). To properly test, delete them and rebuild. Sequence:\n1. Generate asset.\n2. Rewrite RuWordList.kt.\n3. Delete parts.\n4. Update App.kt wiring.\n5. Update gen script.\n6. Update gradle.properties.\n7. Run data unit tests + spotless.\n8. Run app assemble (verify APK size / assets).\n\nLet me check App.kt imports — App.kt uses fully qualified names without import for OcrVocabulary (line 148 `mihon.data.ocr.OcrVocabulary.configure(...)`). I'll match.\n\nNow, before editing App.kt, check that data module APIs are accessible from app (yes—app depends on data).\n\nAlso, does the `data` module's `ru_wordlist.txt` asset get bundled in the *universal/release* APK deliverable? Yes via library asset merge.\n\nAlright, let me implement.\n\nActually — hold on. I should double check one thing about the asset being compressed in APK and read performance: AGP default `androidResources { noCompress }` in app adds tflite/bin to defaults. `.txt` remains compressed. \n\nNow also — the toplevel `app/src/main/assets` is empty, so no conflict with `ocr/ru_wordlist.txt`.\n\nLet me also think: `context.assets.open(ASSET_PATH)` for a compressed txt asset — AssetManager streams it with inflater. All good.\n\nLet me write everything now. Start with a todo list since this is a multi-step task.", "time": {"start": 1791911293967, "end": 1791911334895}, "id": "prt_1363c740f001lKhmEvP1PbJnom", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1363c704e002zbgyoYcsF3J5mm"}, {"type": "text", "text": "\n\n", "time": {"start": 1791911334934, "end": 1791911336913}, "id": "prt_1363d1416001uzJVSobkJyAVkM", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1363c704e002zbgyoYcsF3J5mm"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "todowrite", "callID": "call_3839e1d4144c422ca1981b26", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"todos": [{"content": "Сгенерировать ассет data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt (3 014 492 формы, upper, sorted)", "status": "in_progress", "priority": "high"}, {"content": "Переписать RuWordList.kt: чтение ассета, ленивый build Set, точный capacity, без lowercase", "status": "pending", "priority": "high"}, {"content": "Удалить RuWordListPart*.kt (603 файла)", "status": "pending", "priority": "high"}, {"content": "Проводка RuWordList.configure(context) в App.kt", "status": "pending", "priority": "high"}, {"content": "Обновить scripts/gen_ruwordlist.py на формат ассета", "status": "pending", "priority": "medium"}, {"content": "gradle.properties: вернуть kotlin.daemon.jvmargs 3g + комментарий", "status": "pending", "priority": "low"}, {"content": "Проверка: :data unit tests, :app assembleDebug, spotless", "status": "pending", "priority": "high"}]}, "output": "[\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Сгенерировать ассет data/src/main/assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt (3 014 492 формы, upper, sorted)\",\n    \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Переписать RuWordList.kt: чтение ассета, ленивый build Set, точный capacity, без lowercase\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Удалить RuWordListPart*.kt (603 файла)\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Проводка RuWordList.configure(context) в App.kt\",\n  