fl:N 11340327  84% 1981-01-01 01:01 052b1639  assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt\n", "metadata": {"output": "71110950  Defl:N 11340327  84% 1981-01-01 01:01 052b1639  assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": false}, "title": "grep -i \"ru_wordlist\" /home/runner/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_13662bdb00014ExFenkb8WPU9L", "time": {"start": 1791913810412, "end": 1791913810440}}, "id": "prt_13662d8dd001wG81UKvVaZl0U2", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13662c09b002INvfjpWgtzF1AS"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 122211, "input": 22437, "output": 76, "reasoning": 242, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 99456}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_13662da89001X5s5MdezGa3gMn", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13662c09b002INvfjpWgtzF1AS"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_136627b83001E1n21s9P65Wy1w", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 124797, "input": 407, "output": 282, "reasoning": 2252, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 121856}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791913811311, "completed": 1791913833327}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_13662dd6f0029hba1RHfKAkwdH", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_13662ee370016YGeHHxreUe6zU", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13662dd6f0029hba1RHfKAkwdH"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "It IS deflated: 71,110,950 → 11,340,327 (11.3 MB compressed). So the APK should be ~ rest + 11.3MB. But the APK is 103MB. Let me sum properly. My awk was wrong (columns). Let me compute the real total by listing sizes. Actually `unzip -v` total line at the end gives \"102... \" Let me just trust: APK = 107,767,032 bytes = 102.8 MB. Asset contributes 11.3MB. So the \"rest\" is ~91MB?? That seems high. Original v2.0.0 APK was 87MB total. Now rest = 91MB + asset 11.3 = 102.8. So the \"rest\" grew from 87MB? That can't be — we REMOVED the DEX strings.\n\nWait — maybe the original APK 87MB was the **install size / openWrite size**, which for PackageInstaller `setSize` might be the APK size. Hmm. Actually the crash number 87,103,556 — the TAPK installer sets the session size to the APK size. The v2.0.0 APK on disk. But our debug APK is 103MB. Debug builds differ from release (no R8 minify, no resource shrink). Release APK would be much smaller. The original 87MB was likely the RELEASE APK. Debug is 103MB due to no minification and 19 dex files etc.\n\nSo comparing debug(103MB) to release(87MB) is apples to oranges! I need to compare release-to-release. The old v2.0.0 release APK with R8 = 87MB. Let me build the release APK (assembleRelease) — but it needs signing config; the build.gradle release signingConfig = debug.signingConfig (which may be null if no keystore). Release with `isMinifyEnabled=true` and no signing still produces an unsigned APK in outputs? `assembleRelease` produces app-release-unsigned.apk if no signing. That works for size measurement.\n\nBut this is another 15+ min build. Alternatively, reason about it:\n\nThe release APK = R8-minified + decompressed. In release, the giant DEX string pool would be R8-processed but strings remain; the classes.dex in release would be large but compressed. Removing 65MB of strings from DEX should reduce release APK dramatically.\n\nIn debug, the string-heavy DEX (36MB uncompressed → 9.7MB compressed in classes.dex) — the strings compress well because russian text compresses ~6:1. So in the OLD debug APK, the dictionary added ~10MB compressed (similar to asset's 11.3MB). So debug size barely changed; but RELEASE has R8 which may not compress strings across many dex... Hmm.\n\nWait, this is important. Let me reconsider: Did the original v2.0.0 APK actually contain the 65MB strings as compressed DEX? If DEX compresses 65MB→~10MB, then the original release APK 87MB included only ~10MB for the dictionary, and the total non-dict part is ~77MB?? That doesn't match either — the app without dictionary should be ~20-30MB. \n\nHmm, something is off. Let me reconsider: The debug APK is 103MB with 19 dex files. classes.dex is 36MB uncompressed (contains a lot). Actually the biggest contributions: let me list top entries by compressed size.\n\nWait — maybe I misread: the original crash said 87,103,556 which could be the APK **size reported by TAPK** = maybe not the APK size but the size of the extracted/split APK. Anyway.\n\nLet me step back and actually measure the delta correctly: \n- Before change: the repo had 603 .kt files that compiled into DEX. \n- After: removed, added 71MB asset (compresses to 11.3MB in APK).\n\nTo know if this is a win, I must compare the same build type before/after. I can do that by building release both with and without? That's expensive.\n\nAlternative: reason via DEX. In release, R8/minify: The 65MB of string constants end up in the DEX string data. DEX stores strings as MUTF-8, so ~65MB (close to raw utf8). They compress in the APK zip to maybe 10-12MB (russian text). So dictionary cost in old release APK ≈ 10-12MB. In new release APK, dictionary cost = 11.3MB asset. Essentially THE SAME APK size!\n\nOh no. That means my whole premise was WRONG. The dictionary in DEX was already compressed inside the APK to ~same as gzip. So the APK size doesn't drop 65MB — it barely changes. The 65MB is the UNCOMPRESSED size (install footprint / extracted size), not the APK download size.\n\nBut wait — the crash `Failed to allocate 87103556 because only 0 allocatable` — openWrite size. For a normal PackageInstaller session, the size passed is the APK **file size** (compressed). But the error `only 0 allocatable` — the allocatable space could be about the **uncompressed** required space? Actually installd's free-space check is against the *session size* (the declared sizeBytes = APK file size). Hmm.\n\nHmm, but maybe TAPK's RootlessSaiPackageInstaller sets session size = uncompressed APK size? Or the SAI-like installers compute the size from the APK's uncompressed contents? Actually many installers pass the APK file size. \n\nWait, let me reconsider the original number: 87,103,556 ≈ 83.06 MB. If the old release APK compressed size was ~83MB, and the dictionary compressed to ~11MB, then the rest of the app is ~72MB. That seems large but possible (19 dex, native libs for arm64, fonts, ML models? no models are downloaded). Hmm 72MB is a lot.\n\nAlternatively 87MB might be the **uncompressed** size (APK file on disk is ~87MB because the APK wasn't compressed well — maybe assets are stored uncompressed and dex compressed).\n\nI'm now uncertain about the actual mechanism. The critical question: is the app's install failing because of the APK **file size** (download/staging) or the **installed footprint**? \n\nThe error is from `Session.openWrite(name, offset, length)` where `length` is the total size to write = the APK size being staged. installd checks available space for that length. So it's the APK file size (87MB) that must fit. So the old release APK FILE is ~87MB.\n\nIf our new release APK file is ~same (~87MB or slightly less), we fixed nothing! Because the dictionary already compressed to ~11MB inside the zip.\n\nHmm wait, but then why is the app 87MB? Let me estimate the non-dictionary part. Actually let me look at the largest compressed entries in the debug APK to understand size composition.\n\nThis is critical. Let me get the top 30 largest entries by compressed size from the debug APK, and also compute total.\n\nActually, the debug APK isn't representative (debug has no R8, but it does have compressed dex). Let me look anyway to see biggest items (native libs, dex, asset).\n\nLet me compute top entries.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the OLD build size more concretely. Could I check out the parent commit's state and build? The repo has only one commit (v2.0.0 = HEAD). The .kt files were part of that commit. I deleted them in working tree. I could `git stash` or use `git worktree` to build the old release and compare. That's expensive (2 × ~15min release builds). But it's the only way to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, I can approximate: Build release now (new). Then `git stash` (restore .kt, remove asset) and build release (old). Compare. That's ~30-40 min. Given the importance (the whole task), probably worth it. But maybe there's a faster way to estimate the old APK size: the DEX string data size. Let me reason:\n\nDEX stores string_data as MUTF-8, 65MB total for the forms. In the OLD release APK, those 65MB live in .dex files, which are deflate-compressed in the APK. Russian UTF-8 text deflates ~6-7:1 → ~10MB. So dictionary contributes ~10MB to the old APK file.\n\nNew APK: asset 71MB plain deflates to 11.3MB. So ~equal. Net APK change ≈ 0 to +1MB.\n\nSo we've NOT reduced the APK! The install failure (87MB needed) is dominated by other content, and the dictionary is only ~10MB of the APK file either way.\n\nHmm. But the user reported the APK doesn't install due to space. If the APK is 87MB and dictionary is only 10MB, reducing dictionary helps only ~10MB → 77MB. Still large.\n\nWait, maybe the APK is large because of something else entirely and the dictionary being in DEX bloats it differently. Let me investigate what makes the APK 87-100MB. Let me list largest compressed entries.\n\nActually hold on. Let me reconsider whether DEX compresses as well as I think in a RELEASE build. R8 optimization: The 3M string constants might be kept as string constants. But there's a subtlety: Android's **DEX** has a limit and the strings might be duplicated. Also the `arrayOf` calls create code. But main cost = strings.\n\nLet me look at debug classes.dex: 36MB uncompressed. 9.7MB compressed. The total debug APK is 103MB though. Let me find top contributors.\n\nLet me list entries sorted by compressed size (column 3). The `unzip -v` output format: Length Method Size Cmpr Date Time CRC-32 Name. So column 3 is Size. Let me sort.\n\nLet me run a proper analysis.", "time": {"start": 1791913815675, "end": 1791913831764}, "id": "prt_13662ee7b001Ep6tPuySHUmSXz", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13662dd6f0029hba1RHfKAkwdH"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Важное открытие: ассет в APK всё-таки сжат (71 МБ → 11,3 МБ), а APK получился 103 МБ — то есть в DEX старый словарь, скорее всего, тоже сжимался, и выигрыш неочевиден. Разбираюсь, из чего реально состоит APK.", "time": {"start": 1791913831768, "end": 1791913833125}, "id": "prt_136632d58001QUF64uX0Enpm0N", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13662dd6f0029hba1RHfKAkwdH"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_00_7otwzlh086zvgoxo86eqhi6l", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && unzip -v app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-arm64-v8a-debug.apk 2>/dev/null | awk 'NR>3 && NF>=8 {printf \"%10d  %s\\n\", $3, $8}' | sort -rn | head -25; echo \"--- totals ---\"; unzip -v app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-arm64-v8a-debug.apk 2>/dev/null | awk 'NR>3 && NF>=8 {u+=$1; c+=$3} END{printf \"uncompressed=%.1f MB  compressed=%.1f MB\\n\", u/1048576, c/1048576}'"}, "output": "  11340327  assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt\n  11064544  lib/arm64-v8a/libmlkit_google_ocr_pipeline.so\n   9711724  classes.dex\n   8578647  classes35.dex\n   6056096  resources.arsc\n   5449399  classes38.dex\n   5392000  lib/arm64-v8a/libLiteRt.so\n   5137232  lib/arm64-v8a/libimagedecoder.so\n   4616078  classes36.dex\n   4114438  classes37.dex\n   3811632  lib/arm64-v8a/libtesseract.so\n   2868664  lib/arm64-v8a/libconscrypt_jni.so\n   2827256  lib/arm64-v8a/libLiteRtClGlAccelerator.so\n   2774773  classes39.dex\n   2594056  lib/arm64-v8a/libleptonica.so\n   2031592  lib/arm64-v8a/libarchive-jni.so\n   1906824  lib/arm64-v8a/libhoshidicts_jni.so\n   1065408  lib/arm64-v8a/libsqliteJni.so\n    988408  lib/arm64-v8a/libquickjs.so\n    768712  classes27.dex\n    748767  classes26.dex\n    731872  lib/arm64-v8a/libzstd-kmp.so\n    668495  classes23.dex\n    632050  classes12.dex\n    627604  classes28.dex\n--- totals ---\nuncompressed=241.9 MB  compressed=102.2 MB\n", "metadata": {"output": "  11340327  assets/ocr/ru_wordlist.txt\n  11064544  lib/arm64-v8a/libmlkit_google_ocr_pipeline.so\n   9711724  classes.dex\n   8578647  classes35.dex\n   6056096  resources.arsc\n   5449399  classes38.dex\n   5392000  lib/arm64-v8a/libLiteRt.so\n   5137232  lib/arm64-v8a/libimagedecoder.so\n   4616078  classes36.dex\n   4114438  classes37.dex\n   3811632  lib/arm64-v8a/libtesseract.so\n   2868664  lib/arm64-v8a/libconscrypt_jni.so\n   2827256  lib/arm64-v8a/libLiteRtClGlAccelerator.so\n   2774773  classes39.dex\n   2594056  lib/arm64-v8a/libleptonica.so\n   2031592  lib/arm64-v8a/libarchive-jni.so\n   1906824  lib/arm64-v8a/libhoshidicts_jni.so\n   1065408  lib/arm64-v8a/libsqliteJni.so\n    988408  lib/arm64-v8a/libquickjs.so\n    768712  classes27.dex\n    748767  classes26.dex\n    731872  lib/arm64-v8a/libzstd-kmp.so\n    668495  classes23.dex\n    632050  classes12.dex\n    627604  classes28.dex\n--- totals ---\nuncompressed=241.9 MB  compressed=102.2 MB\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && unzip -v app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-arm64-v8a-debug.apk 2>/dev/null | awk 'NR>3 && NF>=8 {printf \"%10d  %s\\n\", $3, $8}' | sort -rn | head -25; echo \"--- totals ---\"; unzip -v app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-arm64-v8a-debug.apk 2>/dev/null | awk 'NR>3 && NF>=8 {u+=$1; c+=$3} END{printf \"uncompressed=%.1f MB  compressed=%.1f MB\\n\", u/1048576, c/1048576}'", "time": {"start": 1791913833043, "end": 1791913833108}}, "id": "prt_136632f52001Skkhc1IegBgHr4", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13662dd6f0029hba1RHfKAkwdH"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 124797, "input": 407, "output": 282, "reasoning": 2252, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 121856}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_1366332fd001YTuf66G2OQZXjW", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13662dd6f0029hba1RHfKAkwdH"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_136627b83001E1n21s9P65Wy1w", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 127285, "input": 2948, "output": 91, "reasoning": 2006, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 122240}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791913833830, "completed": 1791913855027}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_1366335660020yp5yWbtQ2Qcb5", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_13663489a00180UQ6SylAIZp3f", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366335660020yp5yWbtQ2Qcb5"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "So the debug APK: compressed total 102.2MB. The dictionary asset is 11.3MB. Everything else ~91MB. The library `libmlkit_google_ocr_pipeline.so` is 11MB (bundled ML Kit OCR), tesseract native libs, LiteRT, etc. And 40 dex files.\n\nThe original release APK (v2.0.0) was 87MB — release has R8 (shrinks dex, removes unused). Debug 103MB vs release 87MB is consistent (debug has no shrinking).\n\nNow the key: In the OLD release APK, the dictionary strings were in DEX. How big was that? If DEX compresses strings ~6:1, ~10MB. In the NEW release APK, the asset is 11.3MB. So roughly the same. BUT — is that actually true? Let me test empirically! Let me take the RELEASE build (new) and compare with the OLD release build. But two release builds are expensive.\n\nActually, a cheaper experiment: measure how much the dictionary contributes to the APK in each representation:\n- As asset (new): 11.34MB compressed. Known.\n- As DEX strings (old): I can estimate by creating a dex... hard.\n\nAlternatively, recall the ORIGINAL release APK was 87MB and I can compute: the new release APK. If new release ≈ 87MB minus (old dict dex compressed) plus 11.3MB asset. \n\nHmm. Let me think about whether DEX compresses the strings as well. DEX files in APK ARE deflate-compressed (classes.dex → Defl:N). The strings are MUTF-8, highly compressible. So yes ~6:1.\n\nSo the dictionary cost is ~10-11MB either way. **The APK size barely changes.** My optimization does NOT fix the install problem if the problem is the APK file size.\n\nWait, but then what WAS the install problem? The crash says needs 87,103,556 bytes free. If the APK is 87MB, needing 87MB free is the issue. The APK is 87MB regardless of dict representation. So our change won't help.\n\nHmm, unless... the DEX representation ALSO adds the uncompressed installer footprint. Let me reconsider what installd checks.\n\nActually, I realize I should verify the actual mechanism of `openWrite` size check. The message \"Failed to allocate X because only Y allocatable\" is from **installd** in `InstalldNativeService::openWrite`? Or is it from the **incremental FS**? Let me recall precisely.\n\nActually I now recall: this exact message is from `com.android.server.pm.PackageInstallerService`... no. Let me search memory harder. The phrase \"allocatable\" strongly suggests **`InstalldNativeService::createSession` / `Session::openWrite`** uses `binder` to `installd` which checks the **free space on the /data partition** against the requested session size. The requested size is the APK file size (87MB).\n\nSo to install, device needs roughly the APK file size free (plus some). The APK file size is what matters. Our change doesn't reduce the APK file size meaningfully (both compress the dict similarly).\n\nBUT WAIT. Maybe it does help a lot. Let me reconsider: In the OLD build, the DEX strings total 64.9MB UTF-8. DEX stores them with additional per-string overhead: 3M strings each has a `string_id_item` (4 bytes offset) + `string_data_item` with ULEB128 length prefix + the bytes + null terminator. So ~65MB + 3M*(4 + ~2 + 1) ≈ 65MB + 21MB = 86MB uncompressed DEX string data alone. Plus the `arrayOf` code. Deflate of 86MB russian text ~ maybe 13-15MB. Slightly more than gzip level 9 (which was 8.8MB) because zip deflate default level 6 and the extra structural bytes. So old dict cost in APK ≈ 13-15MB vs new 11.3MB. Saves ~2-4MB. Marginal.\n\nSo this approach barely helps. That's a problem — the user's device fails needing 87MB. Reducing to ~83MB doesn't fix low-storage devices.\n\nHmm. So I may have incorrectly diagnosed. Let me re-examine: Is the APK really 87MB, or is the openWrite size something else?\n\nLet me reconsider TAPK's RootlessSaiPackageInstaller. It likely does:\n```\nsessionParams.setSize(fileSize)  // fileSize = apk length\n...\nsession.openWrite(name, 0, fileSize)\n```\nSo length = APK size = 87MB. The device has 0 allocatable. So the device literally has (almost) 0 bytes free. Even a 30MB APK wouldn't install. But the user says \"v2.0.0 doesn't install\" — maybe older/smaller versions installed fine on that device because they were, say, 40MB, and the device has ~50MB free. v2.0.0 grew to 87MB → fails.\n\nSo we need to make v2.0.0's APK substantially smaller than before. If the dict only accounts for ~13MB, and the old app was ~74MB, then we'd still be at ~74MB — still too big.\n\nWait, this means the app was ALREADY ~70MB+ before the dictionary? That seems suspicious for a manga reader. Unless the APK embeds tesseract + mlkit + LiteRT + all those native libs + 40 dex. Those sum up: mlkit 11MB, LiteRt 5.4MB, libimagedecoder 5.1MB, tesseract 3.8MB, conscrypt 2.8MB, LiteRtClGl 2.8MB, leptonica 2.6MB, archive 2MB, hoshidicts 1.9MB, sqliteJni 1MB, quickjs 1MB, zstd 0.7MB ≈ 42MB of native libs! Plus dex ~40MB compressed... wait dex compressed sizes: 9.7 + 8.6 + 5.4 + 4.6 + 4.1 + 2.8 + smaller ≈ 40MB. Plus resources.arsc 6MB. Plus assets 11.3MB + panel etc. Total ≈ 100MB debug.\n\nSo the app is huge due to native OCR libraries + ML Kit + LiteRT, not just the dictionary.\n\nHmm, so the real solution might need to also address the bundled ML Kit OCR (`libmlkit_google_ocr_pipeline.so` 11MB) which is bundled (text-recognition-bundled?). But that's a bigger change.\n\nOK, I think I've been over-focused. Let me get GROUND TRUTH by measuring the actual delta the change makes to a RELEASE APK. That's the only reliable number, and the user cares about real install size.\n\nPlan:\n1. Build release APK for NEW state (current working tree): `./gradlew :app:assembleRelease`. Get size.\n2. Stash the changes (git stash, which restores .kt files and removes asset), build release again. But wait — changing .kt requires recompiling 3M lines; ~10min extra. Get size.\n3. Compare.\n\nBut actually — is the old release APK size available anywhere? The GitHub release v2.0.0 asset size! The repo is sj0404-collab/yomikai. I could query the GitHub releases API for the v2.0.0 APK asset size. That's the real released artifact size! Let me do that. `gh release view v2.0.0 --repo sj0404-collab/yomikai --json assets`. But network + auth. Let me try.\n\nActually the repo might be private. Let me try `gh`.\n\nLet me try fetching release info.\n\nAlso, the crash number 87,103,556 might exactly equal the released APK size. If the GitHub release asset size ≈ 87,103,556, that confirms the old release APK is 87MB. Then I build the new release and compare.\n\nLet me try gh / curl.\n\nHmm, but even better: maybe I don't need release build. Let me just check: The number 87103556. If that's the release APK size, then to fix we need new release < that by enough margin. Let me measure new release.\n\nGiven time constraints, let me build the new release APK now. But release signing: release build uses `signingConfig = debug.signingConfig`; if no keystore env, `debug.signingConfig` may be null → release unsigned. assembleRelease will produce unsigned APK (or fail if signing required?). Since signingConfig = debug.signingConfig may be null, it's fine (unsigned output).\n\nActually release also needs `isMinifyEnabled=true`. R8 with fullMode=false. Could be slow. Let's do it.\n\nBut first, let me check GitHub for the v2.0.0 asset size to confirm the baseline.", "time": {"start": 1791913838761, "end": 1791913853677}, "id": "prt_1366348a9001pTKytKw5leObmM", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366335660020yp5yWbtQ2Qcb5"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_00_yjhwyj5fv4hnofgsw7oyzakg", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && (gh release view v2.0.0 --repo sj0404-collab/yomikai --json tagName,assets 2>&1 | head -40) || echo \"gh failed\""}, "output": "{\"assets\":[{\"apiUrl\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/sj0404-collab/yomikai/releases/assets/637634263\",\"contentType\":\"text/markdown\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-13T16:43:07Z\",\"digest\":\"sha256:f38dd148e9e11cea776a798416b2c754601b4d62a5aa8626b5b98df273c154b1\",\"downloadCount\":0,\"id\":\"RA_kwDOT5KVMs4mAYbX\",\"label\":\"\",\"name\":\"OCR-QUALITY-REPORT-16326b93f0888d0ac471f9891457df02c58b5164.md\",\"size\":4632,\"state\":\"uploaded\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-13T16:43:07Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/sj0404-collab/yomikai/releases/download/v2.0.0/OCR-QUALITY-REPORT-16326b93f0888d0ac471f9891457df02c58b5164.md\"},{\"apiUrl\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/sj0404-collab/yomikai/releases/assets/637634270\",\"contentType\":\"application/vnd.android.package-archive\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-13T16:43:07Z\",\"digest\":\"sha256:be7a3618e233b148da075696fdd65a44802e744f93b3c55a1acc6036ccc72152\",\"downloadCount\":6,\"id\":\"RA_kwDOT5KVMs4mAYbe\",\"label\":\"\",\"name\":\"yomikai-v2.0.0.apk\",\"size\":87103556,\"state\":\"uploaded\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-13T16:43:14Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/sj0404-collab/yomikai/releases/download/v2.0.0/yomikai-v2.0.0.apk\"}],\"tagName\":\"v2.0.0\"}\n", "metadata": {"output": "{\"assets\":[{\"apiUrl\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/sj0404-collab/yomikai/releases/assets/637634263\",\"contentType\":\"text/markdown\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-13T16:43:07Z\",\"digest\":\"sha256:f38dd148e9e11cea776a798416b2c754601b4d62a5aa8626b5b98df273c154b1\",\"downloadCount\":0,\"id\":\"RA_kwDOT5KVMs4mAYbX\",\"label\":\"\",\"name\":\"OCR-QUALITY-REPORT-16326b93f0888d0ac471f9891457df02c58b5164.md\",\"size\":4632,\"state\":\"uploaded\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-13T16:43:07Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/sj0404-collab/yomikai/releases/download/v2.0.0/OCR-QUALITY-REPORT-16326b93f0888d0ac471f9891457df02c58b5164.md\"},{\"apiUrl\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/sj0404-collab/yomikai/releases/assets/637634270\",\"contentType\":\"application/vnd.android.package-archive\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-13T16:43:07Z\",\"digest\":\"sha256:be7a3618e233b148da075696fdd65a44802e744f93b3c55a1acc6036ccc72152\",\"downloadCount\":6,\"id\":\"RA_kwDOT5KVMs4mAYbe\",\"label\":\"\",\"name\":\"yomikai-v2.0.0.apk\",\"size\":87103556,\"state\":\"uploaded\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-13T16:43:14Z\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/sj0404-collab/yomikai/releases/download/v2.0.0/yomikai-v2.0.0.apk\"}],\"tagName\":\"v2.0.0\"}\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && (gh release view v2.0.0 --repo sj0404-collab/yomikai --json tagName,assets 2>&1 | head -40) || echo \"gh failed\"", "time": {"start": 1791913854038, "end": 1791913854807}}, "id": "prt_1366382f10015GbtHXmc7FJmjz", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366335660020yp5yWbtQ2Qcb5"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 127285, "input": 2948, "output": 91, "reasoning": 2006, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 122240}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_1366387b7001rolLHNEOYAWodX", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366335660020yp5yWbtQ2Qcb5"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_136627b83001E1n21s9P65Wy1w", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 128914, "input": 2564, "output": 190, "reasoning": 976, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 125184}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791913855745, "completed": 1791913869129}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_136638b01002hXuobrTKQxWvjQ", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_136639b6a001jbeXyF3CLzuNKB", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136638b01002hXuobrTKQxWvjQ"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "Confirmed: the released `yomikai-v2.0.0.apk` size = **87,103,556 bytes** — exactly the number in the crash. So the crash is because the APK file is 87MB and the device has no room to stage it.\n\nSo the OLD (current released) release APK = 87,103,556. It already has R8 minification. The dictionary is inside DEX.\n\nNow I need to build the NEW release APK and see the size. If our change makes it smaller, great; if ~same, we haven't fixed it.\n\nLet me build `:app:assembleRelease`. Note the release APK is arm64-v8a only (splits). Let me run.\n\nAlso — I realize the debug APK (103MB) with no R8 vs release (87MB) is consistent.\n\nLet me build release and measure. Might take a while, reuse daemon/cache.\n\nActually before spending 15 min, let me estimate the dictionary's contribution in the released APK more rigorously. In the released APK, DEX is R8-minified (fullMode=false) — R8 does NOT strip string constants. The strings remain. classes.dex etc. compress. \n\nRough: old dict in DEX ~ uncompressed 86MB → compressed maybe ~13MB. New asset 11.3MB. So new release APK ≈ 87 - 13 + 11.3 ≈ 85.3MB. Only ~1.7MB smaller. That wouldn't fix install.\n\nHmm. That's bad. So the whole approach doesn't meaningfully reduce the APK. \n\nWait — but is it possible the released APK stored the DEX **uncompressed**? Modern Android APKs: `classes.dex` may be stored uncompressed to allow direct mmap (extractNativeLibs / useEmbeddedDex). If dex files are `Stored` (uncompressed) in the APK, then the 86MB dictionary would make the APK ~86MB+! And indeed the released APK is 87MB — which matches the dictionary uncompressed size almost exactly + a bit! \n\nLet me check the DEBUG apk: classes.dex showed `Defl:N` (compressed). But debug may differ. For RELEASE, AGP might store dex uncompressed? Actually by default, AGP compresses dex unless `android:extractNativeLibs`/`useLegacyPackaging`. Hmm. But the released APK total 87MB vs debug 103MB. If release dex were uncompressed, release would be BIGGER than debug, not smaller. Since release (87) < debug(103), release dex is compressed (R8 shrinks + compression). \n\nLet me compute what the release APK would be without the dictionary: If dict contributes ~13MB compressed, non-dict ≈ 74MB. With native libs ~42MB + resources 6MB + dex (rest) etc. Plausible.\n\nHmm, so 74MB base. Still huge. To make installs work on low-storage devices, we'd need to cut much more.\n\nWait, but maybe I'm wrong about dict contributing only 13MB. Let me actually MEASURE by building the release with and without. The \"with\" (old) size is known: 87,103,556. So I just need the \"without\" (new) size. Build release now. If new ≈ 87 - X, X tells us the benefit. Let's do it.\n\nActually, I can get the answer faster: I don't need full R8. The dictionary's compressed contribution can be measured from the debug APK delta: debug has asset 11.3MB compressed. If I remove the asset and rebuild debug... but I can't easily remove it and the old debug had the .kt (which I deleted). Ugh.\n\nSimplest reliable: build release new. Let me just do it. ~15min.\n\nLet me run assembleRelease.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider the possibility that releases store dex uncompressed. Let me check the actual released APK by downloading it (downloadCount 6, public?). `gh release download v2.0.0 -p '*.apk'`. Then inspect its entries with unzip -v to see how classes.dex is stored and where the 87MB goes. THAT is the most informative and faster than a build! Let me download the released APK and analyze.\n\nYes — download the actual released APK and dissect it. That tells us exactly what to cut. Let me do that.", "time": {"start": 1791913860004, "end": 1791913866554}, "id": "prt_136639ba4001XFkF0CNYE2PVC5", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136638b01002hXuobrTKQxWvjQ"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Ключевой факт: релизный APK v2.0.0 ровно `87,103,556` байт — это и есть число из краша. Скачаю сам релиз и разберу, из чего он состоит.", "time": {"start": 1791913866562, "end": 1791913867593}, "id": "prt_13663b541001VvIHbqu6yVHf6p", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136638b01002hXuobrTKQxWvjQ"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_00_2r4rgt08po47lajrgg6qpjut", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp/opencode && rm -f yomikai-v2.0.0.apk && gh release download v2.0.0 --repo sj0404-collab/yomikai --pattern '*.apk' --dir /tmp/opencode --clobber 2>&1 | tail -5; ls -la /tmp/opencode/*.apk", "timeout": 300000}, "output": "-rw-r--r-- 1 runner runner 87103556 Oct 13 17:51 /tmp/opencode/yomikai-v2.0.0.apk\n", "metadata": {"output": "-rw-r--r-- 1 runner runner 87103556 Oct 13 17:51 /tmp/opencode/yomikai-v2.0.0.apk\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /tmp/opencode && rm -f yomikai-v2.0.0.apk && gh release download v2.0.0 --repo sj0404-collab/yomikai --pattern '*.apk' --dir /tmp/opencode --clobber 2