tep-finish", "tokens": {"total": 129141, "input": 1219, "output": 178, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 127744}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_13663da99001vbf8N1NcXJ8m9s", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13663c3c5002JKnZX803aQOpF2"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_136627b83001E1n21s9P65Wy1w", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 130884, "input": 897, "output": 234, "reasoning": 857, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 128896}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791913877165, "completed": 1791913893782}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_13663dead002BnHhVsMzORkmbC", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_13663f06d001UxMara8Uj3r1o6", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13663dead002BnHhVsMzORkmbC"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "Now this is very informative. In the RELEASED v2.0.0 APK:\n- `classes4.dex` = **30,163,093** bytes (compressed) — this is the giant DEX containing the RuWordList strings! It's the largest entry. (Note: earlier `unzip -v` shows \"Length\" column 1 and \"Size\" column 3; my awk prints $3 = compressed size. So classes4.dex compressed = 30.16MB.)\n- Total compressed = 82.7MB (the 87MB includes zip central directory / signing block overhead ~4MB).\n\nSo the dictionary DEX (classes4.dex) is 30MB COMPRESSED in the release APK! Why so big compressed? Because DEX string data with 3M strings doesn't compress as well as raw concatenated text (interleaved offsets, ULEB lengths, null terminators, and possibly the strings are not contiguous — DEX string_data section may order strings and have entropy). Actually the compressed 30MB for ~86MB uncompressed = 2.9:1, worse than our gzip 8.8MB for 68MB text (7.7:1). The difference: DEX layout breaks long runs, and R8 might not have removed anything.\n\nWait — but is classes4.dex ONLY the dictionary? 30MB compressed for strings that as plain gzipped text are 8.8MB. The DEX overhead + poor layout inflates it ~3.4x. Regardless, in the RELEASE APK the dictionary effectively costs ~30MB!\n\nSo replacing it with an 11.3MB compressed asset saves ~30 - 11.3 = **~19MB** in the APK. New release APK ≈ 87 - 19 ≈ 68MB. That's meaningful but maybe not enough for the failing device.\n\nBut wait — why is classes4.dex 30MB compressed when the raw text gzips to 8.8MB? Let me verify classes4.dex is the dict. It's plausible R8 put the 3M strings there. The compression delta is suspicious but DEX string data has lots of structure. Also maybe the strings are uppercase+lowercase? No, only lowercase in source; but Kotlin compiler may intern. Hmm.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: maybe classes4.dex contains the array construction code `arrayOf(...)` in 603 functions. `arrayOf` of 3M strings creates bytecode with 3M `const-string` instructions (each referencing a string index) + array fills. R8 might keep the methods. The code is large. Also string_data section. So 30MB compressed.\n\nAnyway, the empirical fix: remove classes4.dex (30MB) → add asset (11.3MB) → save ~19MB. New release ~68MB.\n\nIs 68MB enough? The failing device had 0 allocatable when needing 87MB. We don't know its total free space. If it had, say, 70MB free, 68MB might just fit (needs ~68MB + staging overhead). If it had 40MB free, still fails.\n\nHmm, but this is a big improvement (87→68, -22%). Combined with the fact that debug APK also dropped? Let me verify by building the new release. Actually, I can estimate more precisely from the debug comparison: debug old would have had classes.dex with the strings. But I deleted the .kt; I can't build old easily. But I have the released old APK. Let me build new release and compare directly.\n\nBefore building, let me double check classes4.dex content by extracting and looking at strings — confirm it's the wordlist. Let me grep the dex for a known word \"АБДУЛАХАДОВИЧАМ\". Actually compressed dex inside zip; `unzip -p ... classes4.dex | strings | grep`. Let me verify.\n\nLet me confirm classes4.dex holds the dictionary.", "time": {"start": 1791913881781, "end": 1791913887780}, "id": "prt_13663f0b5001TeA4CjO05sfuzo", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13663dead002BnHhVsMzORkmbC"}, {"type": "text", "text": "`classes4.dex` = 30 МБ (сжатый) — вот он, словарь. Проверю, что это именно он, и посчитаю реальный выигрыш.", "time": {"start": 1791913887786, "end": 1791913888860}, "id": "prt_13664082a001rmRur2btaXNeD8", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13663dead002BnHhVsMzORkmbC"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_00_yshwsx42znxru7m5x57291xh", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp/opencode && unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk classes4.dex 2>/dev/null | strings | grep -c -i \"абдулахадович\\|КАКЖЕ\\|БАСКЕРВИЛЬ\" ; echo \"--- sample ---\"; unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk classes4.dex 2>/dev/null | strings | grep -i \"баскервиль\\|абдулахадович\" | head -3; echo \"--- dex compressed size ---\"; unzip -v yomikai-v2.0.0.apk 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"classes4.dex\""}, "output": "0\n--- sample ---\n--- dex compressed size ---\n140804312  Defl:N 30163093  79% 1981-01-01 01:01 3daa854a  classes4.dex\n", "metadata": {"output": "0\n--- sample ---\n--- dex compressed size ---\n140804312  Defl:N 30163093  79% 1981-01-01 01:01 3daa854a  classes4.dex\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /tmp/opencode && unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk classes4.dex 2>/dev/null | strings | grep -c -i \"абдулахадович\\|КАКЖЕ\\|БАСКЕРВИЛЬ\" ; echo \"--- sample ---\"; unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk classes4.dex 2>/dev/null | strings | grep -i \"баскервиль\\|абдулахадович\" | head -3; echo \"--- dex compressed size ---\"; unzip -v yomikai-v2.0.0.apk 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"classes4.dex\"", "time": {"start": 1791913888801, "end": 1791913893556}}, "id": "prt_1366409270011lGCCrzTTyDzON", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13663dead002BnHhVsMzORkmbC"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 130884, "input": 897, "output": 234, "reasoning": 857, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 128896}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_136641f1d0014Vjb3wQZQAWBTj", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_13663dead002BnHhVsMzORkmbC"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_136627b83001E1n21s9P65Wy1w", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"total": 131637, "input": 1153, "output": 167, "reasoning": 525, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 129792}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791913894351, "completed": 1791913905607}, "finish": "tool-calls", "id": "msg_1366421cf002D1DVIgEbV3RHCd", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_13664325e001pzHnUdBvt6imJU", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366421cf002D1DVIgEbV3RHCd"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "Interesting! `classes4.dex` uncompressed = 140,804,312 bytes (~134MB!) compressed to 30.16MB. But grep for \"абдулахадович\" found 0. Because strings in DEX are MUTF-8 but maybe the words are lowercase (source was lowercase). I grepped case-insensitive for lowercase patterns too (\"абдулахадович\" lowercase). Got 0. Hmm. Maybe the strings are compressed in dex? No. Or maybe classes4.dex is something else (e.g., ML Kit models?), and the dictionary is spread across classes3.dex (4.4MB compressed) etc.\n\nWait, 140MB uncompressed dex! That's the giant one. It must contain the 3M strings. But `strings` didn't find \"абдулахадович\". Let me try other words, or check if dex strings are stored with different encoding. Actually DEX string_data is MUTF-8, `strings` should find ASCII/Cyrillic UTF-8 sequences. Unless the dex is further compressed (it's not, dex isn't internally compressed). Hmm.\n\nMaybe my `strings` grep failed because the words are uppercase in one dex and lowercase in another, and classes4 contains something else. Let me search across ALL dex for a rare word.\n\nLet me extract all dex and grep for \"баскервиль\" (case-insensitive) and \"БАСКЕРВИЛЬ\". Also try \"содержала\".\n\nLet me do a robust search: unzip -p each classes*.dex | grep -a -o -i \"баскервиль\" | head.\n\nActually, let me just search the whole APK binary for the word (compressed entries won't match, so need to decompress). Let me loop over dex files.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the RuWordList strings were **obfuscated/optimized away**?? No, they're used.\n\nLet me just check classes4 with `strings -n 6` for Cyrillic. Actually `strings` default only prints ASCII sequences (>=4 printable ASCII). Cyrillic UTF-8 bytes are non-ASCII → `strings` won't print them! That's why 0 matches. Need `strings -e` or just grep the raw bytes.\n\nSo grep raw: `unzip -p ... classes4.dex | grep -a -c \"баскервиль\"` (binary grep). Let me do that.", "time": {"start": 1791913898639, "end": 1791913902546}, "id": "prt_13664328f001NS3v3TJPw9tIbP", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366421cf002D1DVIgEbV3RHCd"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_00_g9m7ultqqqypntlufxk7pg31", "state": {"status": "completed", "input": {"command": "cd /tmp/opencode && for d in classes4.dex classes3.dex classes2.dex classes.dex; do c=$(unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk $d 2>/dev/null | grep -a -c \"БАСКЕРВИЛЬ\"); echo \"$d: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=$c\"; done; echo \"--- lowercase in classes4 ---\"; unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk classes4.dex 2>/dev/null | grep -a -c \"абдулахадович\""}, "output": "classes4.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=1\nclasses3.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=0\nclasses2.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=0\nclasses.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=0\n--- lowercase in classes4 ---\n1\n", "metadata": {"output": "classes4.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=1\nclasses3.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=0\nclasses2.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=0\nclasses.dex: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=0\n--- lowercase in classes4 ---\n1\n", "exit": 0, "truncated": false}, "title": "cd /tmp/opencode && for d in classes4.dex classes3.dex classes2.dex classes.dex; do c=$(unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk $d 2>/dev/null | grep -a -c \"БАСКЕРВИЛЬ\"); echo \"$d: БАСКЕРВИЛЬ matches=$c\"; done; echo \"--- lowercase in classes4 ---\"; unzip -p yomikai-v2.0.0.apk classes4.dex 2>/dev/null | grep -a -c \"абдулахадович\"", "time": {"start": 1791913903337, "end": 1791913905466}}, "id": "prt_1366441d6001wtaTldBhAVUbVZ", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366421cf002D1DVIgEbV3RHCd"}, {"reason": "tool-calls", "snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-finish", "tokens": {"total": 131637, "input": 1153, "output": 167, "reasoning": 525, "cache": {"write": 0, "read": 129792}}, "cost": 0, "id": "prt_136644d7e001ov655hYs0IkLXN", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_1366421cf002D1DVIgEbV3RHCd"}]}, {"info": {"parentID": "msg_136627b83001E1n21s9P65Wy1w", "role": "assistant", "mode": "build", "agent": "build", "path": {"cwd": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code", "root": "/home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code"}, "cost": 0, "tokens": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "reasoning": 0, "cache": {"read": 0, "write": 0}}, "modelID": "big-pickle", "providerID": "opencode", "time": {"created": 1791913906212}, "id": "msg_136645024002yMnyfYbpQ8Nin5", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r"}, "parts": [{"snapshot": "b5444c1210892cd71c3c4a5200538d26e37a3438", "type": "step-start", "id": "prt_136645d96001FX9AS7yWURZl8L", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136645024002yMnyfYbpQ8Nin5"}, {"type": "reasoning", "text": "Confirmed: `classes4.dex` contains the dictionary (lowercase and uppercase via seeds; the forms are lowercase and uppercase built at runtime, but \"БАСКЕРВИЛЬ\" appears because SEEDS/regression tokens are uppercase in source? Actually the generator lowercases seeds; but there may be uppercase literals from BEFORE... anyway it contains it).\n\nSo classes4.dex: uncompressed 140.8MB → compressed 30.16MB. That's the dictionary DEX (plus array code). Our asset replaces it with 11.34MB compressed. Savings ≈ 30.16 - 11.34 = **18.8MB**.\n\nBut wait: the uncompressed 140.8MB is huge — 65MB of string bytes become 140MB dex? Because DEX string_data includes ULEB length + bytes, string_ids 4 bytes each, plus the `const-string` instructions in 603 methods (3M instructions × ~3 bytes) and array fill. So DEX inflates a lot. Compressed 30MB.\n\nNow new release APK ≈ 87.1 - 18.8 = **68.3MB**. That's a solid reduction (-22%). But is it enough? Unknown. The device that failed needs 68MB free now. It's better.\n\nHmm, but I should aim higher. The user said \"не устанавливается\" — if the device had e.g. 50MB free, 68MB still fails. But maybe the device had ~80MB and 87 failed; 68 would succeed.\n\nBut actually — there might be MORE low-hanging fruit. The big items: `libmlkit_google_ocr_pipeline.so` 11MB, LiteRt 5.4MB, libimagedecoder 5.1MB, tesseract 3.8MB, etc. Plus the mlkit-google-ocr-models assets. But the project depends on built-in OCR; removing ML Kit would degrade features. The user wants no degradation. So keep.\n\nSo the main win is the dictionary (18.8MB). Given our constraint (no functional/perf regression), that's the right change.\n\nActually, we can do better on the dictionary too: our asset compresses to 11.34MB. Could we compress more? Options:\n- Store a **gzip** file (gzip level 9 = 8.79MB) as asset, but then the APK would store it... if we name it `.gz`, AGP might store it compressed again (double) — no benefit, and runtime double-decompresses. If we ensure it's NOT recompressed (noCompress \"gz\"), APK stores 8.79MB and runtime gunzips once → 8.79MB in APK (vs 11.34MB for plain text). Saves another 2.5MB. But adds runtime gunzip (the user's speed concern). Net APK 68.3 - 2.5 = ~65.8MB.\n- Or build a more compact binary format (e.g., sorted words in UTF-8, no newlines, or front-coded). But gzip already captures most.\n\nGiven the user's \"don't degrade speed\" priority, the plain-text asset (no extra decompress step) is the safer choice. The 2.5MB difference is minor vs the 18.8MB. Stick with plain text.\n\nBut hold on — let me reconsider the runtime cost of the plain asset vs old DEX. In the old release, RuWordList.upper built a HashSet from 603 arrays of DEX strings (no I/O). New: read 71MB from asset (deflated in zip, inflated on the fly) + split lines + insert. The inflation of 71MB and 3M `readLine()` calls. That's the added cost. On device maybe 0.5-1.5s one-time on background thread. The user accepted this (\"если ничего по скорости не критично\"). It's one-time and off the main thread. Acceptable. And we removed 3M `uppercase()` calls, partially offsetting.\n\nNow, let me VERIFY the new release APK size by building it. That's the key deliverable. Build `:app:assembleRelease`.\n\nAlso I should double check the debug asset compressed 11.34MB, and release similar. Let's build release.\n\nAlso, note: the released APK has NO `assets/ocr/` obviously. Good.\n\nOne more consideration: the release build in CI uses `release.yml`/`release-universal.yml` — does the CI build via Gradle and does it include our asset automatically? Yes, asset is in the data module → merged.\n\nLet me build release now and measure. Might take ~15 min.\n\nActually — before that, do I even need the full release build? I have strong evidence: savings = old classes4.dex compressed (30.16MB) - new asset compressed (~11.3MB) ≈ 18.8MB. New release ≈ 68.3MB. But to be safe and give the user a real number, build it.\n\nLet me run assembleRelease. It may complain about signing (release signingConfig = debug.signingConfig, possibly null). Let's try.\n\nLet me also confirm the app's `noCompress` doesn't include our asset extension — it's .txt, compressed as seen (11.3MB). Good.\n\nRun release build.", "time": {"start": 1791913909692, "end": 1791913917814}, "id": "prt_136645dbc0018Qh7CTMHMwrk4l", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136645024002yMnyfYbpQ8Nin5"}, {"type": "text", "text": "Подтверждено: `classes4.dex` (словарь) — **140,8 МБ несжато / 30,16 МБ в APK**. Замена ассетом (11,3 МБ) должна срезать ~19 МБ. Собираю релиз для точного замера.", "time": {"start": 1791913917818, "end": 1791913918597}, "id": "prt_136647d7a001w85qQU8VH5dq7T", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136645024002yMnyfYbpQ8Nin5"}, {"type": "tool", "tool": "bash", "callID": "call_00_9c2425uk5zcb2dtkz1sgrhxa", "state": {"metadata": {"output": ""}, "status": "running", "input": {"command": "cd /home/runner/hub-work/yomikai/code && ./gradlew :app:assembleRelease --console=plain 2>&1 | tail -25", "timeout": 2400000}, "time": {"start": 1791913918590}}, "id": "prt_136647f50001zDETpI09o7Q34b", "sessionID": "ses_ec9cf465fffebOZ3QlKFLFfp4r", "messageID": "msg_136645024002yMnyfYbpQ8Nin5"}]}]}}]}